  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000) alone achieves 0.485 acc while image (resnet50) alone is only 0.208, and the multimodal model (config_018) reaches 0.523—only a ~4% gain over RNA alone. This indicates RNA is the dominant signal and the current linear PCA representation may be a bottleneck. Uncertainty: We have only tested a linear RNA encoder (pca_n2000); it is unknown whether a learned encoder (scgpt) captures non-linear biological structure that would substantially improve both the RNA baseline and the multimodal model. This experiment (config_007: multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, resnet50, weighted fusion) changes exactly one variable relative to config_018—the RNA encoder—so the result cleanly isolates the effect of RNA representation quality. If scgpt yields a meaningful accuracy/F1 gain over config_018, it tells us the RNA representation is the primary lever for improvement and justifies further investment in learned encoders; if not, PCA is near-sufficient and we should pivot to image encoder quality or fusion strategy. Under a limited budget, testing the dominant modality's representation first is the highest-information single experiment."
}

